[Exact verifier](../../research/verify_threshold_cut_torque_2026_10_02.py):
square over Q and regular hexagon over Q(sqrt(3)). It checks all pair lengths,
actual contact/diameter sets, normalized positive full vertex equilibrium,
Omega^2=2 Omega and its affine kernel, every chosen opposite-side cut,
CT.1 and the complete matrix (13), nonzero peripheral contact variance,
and invariance under a translated origin. The general lever budget, conditional
threshold corollary, and all-even-q construction have the analytic proofs above.
Finite computations do not establish global optimality or an unbounded
global-minimizer family. The shell regression does not encode the complete
O--O rectangle, full mixed rigidity, or finite feasibility of any train move.

