## 7. Exact remaining gap and disposition

The next source obligation is a **spatial estimate on the actual positive
contact-port measure beyond its first moment** (or a finite move bypassing
that measure), using the linear complete rectangle and canonical mixed
rigidity. The attempted centroid and moment-Gram implications were tested
and failed, rather than left as presumed closing lemmas. CT.2 remains a valid
additive reaction constraint for a different co-embedding argument.

This packet eliminates no global branch. Threshold and open-cell exact phase,
nonconstant phase, split-star O--O, inactive interfaces, macroscopic inactive
containers/exterior caps, and higher-surplus full-core sources all remain open.
The canonical manifest, route map and prompt are unchanged. Promotion
recommendation: preserve unreviewed, independently audit CT.1--CT.3/CM.1,
and require the full promotion transaction before using any new claim as canonical.
